# Git & Deploy

## Git
- Remote: `https://github.com/dybydx/html-catalog.git`
- Default branch: `main`
- Only commit when the user explicitly asks
- Never update git config, force-push main, or skip hooks

## Commit message style
One concise sentence focused on **why**, e.g.:
```
Make category sidebar sticky on large screens.
```

## Deploy to Cloudflare Pages
After push (when requested):
```bash
wrangler pages deploy . --project-name=html-catalog --branch=main
```

- **No build command** — static files deploy from project root
- Production URL: https://html-catalog.pages.dev
- Cloudflare account: WebWeaver

## What not to deploy
- `.git/`, `.cursor/` (not part of site assets anyway)
- Secrets or `.env` files
